 ## Overview
-Gaussian Splatting Initialization and Parameterization establishes the initial state of the 3D Gaussian primitives ($\mathcal{G}$) from a sparse Structure-from-Motion (SfM) point cloud, providing geometrically accurate starting positions, colors, and covariances [S2, S8, unofficial]. Unlike random initialization, which lacks normal information and accurate geometry, SfM initialization leverages multi-view matching to produce a sparse cloud that serves as a superior prior for the differentiable renderer, significantly improving reconstruction quality and convergence speed [S7, S8, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from dense MVS initialization by avoiding the baking of MVS errors and redundant geometry, relying instead on the optimizer to create detail during training [S8, unofficial].
+Gaussian Splatting Initialization and Parameterization establishes the initial state of the 3D Gaussian primitives ($\mathcal{G}$) from a sparse Structure-from-Motion (SfM) point cloud, providing geometrically accurate starting positions, colors, and covariances [S2, S8, unofficial]. SfM initialization produces a sparse point cloud that may not cover all geometry, whereas random initialization is denser but lacks normals and accurate initial positions; SfM is preferred if 2D images are available [S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from dense MVS initialization by avoiding the baking of MVS errors and redundant geometry, relying instead on the optimizer to create detail during training [S8, unofficial].
 
