 ### Neural Point Cloud Initialization from COLMAP
-A method to initialize the neural point cloud and their features for Point-NeRF using an external point cloud reconstruction (specifically COLMAP). It solves the problem of how to provide initial positions, variances, and feature vectors for the neural points. The variance parameter $\gamma_i$ for each point $p_i$ is initialized to 0.3. To acquire the feature vector $f_i$ for a point $p_i$, views where the point is occluded are ruled out, and the view closest to the point is selected. The point is unprojected onto the feature maps extracted by a 2D CNN to obtain $f_i$ [S9].
