 ### Single Ellipsoid Initialization
-Initializes a single ellipsoid from a set of 3D points using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to determine orientation, center, and radii. The minimum allowed radius $r_{\min}$ is typically 0.005 to avoid numerical problems, and a scaling factor $\alpha$ (typically 3) ensures points are mostly covered [S11].
+Initializes a single ellipsoid from a set of 3D points using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to determine orientation, center, and radii [S12]. The minimum allowed radius $r_{\min}$ is typically 0.005 to avoid numerical problems, and a scaling factor $\alpha$ (typically 3) ensures points are mostly covered [S12].
 
 ### MVS-guided Initialization
-Aggregates filtered multiview depth maps from an MVS method into a unified 3D point cloud. An initial optimization phase prunes noisy Gaussians by freezing centers and optimizing other parameters for $N_{prun}$ iterations, removing Gaussians with opacity $\alpha_k < \tau$. Afterward, all parameters are unfrozen for standard optimization with Adaptive Density Control [S12].
